From 8e3b2815382005e7464ec9c8d18bc67286722973 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Hughes <ryan@heyoodle.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:58:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] HID: asus: disable OOBE mode on the ProArt P14 keyboard too

The ProArt P14 H7407BA's 0B05:4B42 keyboard starts in the same OOBE mode
as the ProArt P16's: once it takes the init handshake its backlight keeps
fading in and out on its own and ignores the level the host sets. The
OOBE disable sequence already sent on the P16 stops it, so send it when
the DMI product family is "ProArt P14" as well.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/hid/hid-asus.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-asus.c b/drivers/hid/hid-asus.c
index 1b28a5d9f..2fe6ac299 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-asus.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-asus.c
@@ -803,7 +803,8 @@ static int asus_kbd_register_leds(struct hid_device *hdev)
 		asus_kbd_init(hdev, FEATURE_KBD_LED_REPORT_ID2);
 	}
 
-	if (dmi_match(DMI_PRODUCT_FAMILY, "ProArt P16")) {
+	if (dmi_match(DMI_PRODUCT_FAMILY, "ProArt P16") ||
+	    dmi_match(DMI_PRODUCT_FAMILY, "ProArt P14")) {
 		ret = asus_kbd_disable_oobe(hdev);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
-- 
2.56.0

